course: dictionary
lesson: 4499
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Haw» is a good example: it can be a red berry, a way to take a long time to decide, a loud laugh, or a call to a farm animal. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is right.
explain: Look at the words next to it. If a sentence talks about berries and birds, haw means a berry. If it talks about someone who cannot decide, «hum and haw» means taking a long time to choose. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: The donkey sentence uses haw as a sound. «The «hee» is breathed in and the «haw» breathed out» means a donkey's bray has two parts: hee when it breathes in, and haw when it breathes out. Here haw is a sound, not a word for a thing.
fact: A haw is a small red berry that grows on the hawthorn tree.
fact: «Hum and haw» means to take a long time to decide, making sounds like «um» and «er».
fact: «Haw haw» is the sound of a loud laugh, often written in comics.
fact: On a farm, «haw!» tells a horse or ox to turn left, and «gee» tells it to turn right.
fact: In a donkey's bray, the «haw» is the sound breathed out, after the «hee» breathed in.
exercise: In winter, blackbirds ate the haws from the hawthorn hedge. What is a haw? | A farm call to turn left | A donkey's ear | A loud laugh | *A small red berry
exercise: Ben could not choose, so he began to hum and haw over the menu. What does hum and haw mean? | To sing a tune loudly | To laugh at a joke | *To take a long time to decide | To turn left
exercise: Farmer Jo shouted, «Haw!» to the ox. Which way did the ox turn? | Right | *Left | Up the hill | Backwards
test: The children laughed, «haw haw», at the silly clown. What does «haw haw» show? | A sad sigh | A call to a horse to go faster | A small red berry | *A loud laugh
test: Which word is the farm call to a horse or ox to turn right? | Laugh | Berry | *Gee | Haw
exam: In a donkey's hee-haw bray, which sound is breathed out? | *Haw | Both sounds | Hee | Neither sound
